./README.md:11:## Reproduce
./README.md:34:Code: MIT License (see `LICENSE`). Data compiled from the Banco Central del Ecuador are public; third-party series (FRED, Baumeister and Hamilton, 2019; Känzig, 2021) remain the property of their providers and are included, with attribution, only as the vintages needed to reproduce the paper; the VIX (© Cboe) is downloaded, not redistributed.
./README_REPLICATION.md:27:The Baumeister–Hamilton shock series is revised and extended periodically at its source (the paper uses the vintage ending in 2026:03, retrieved 2026-09-26). To reproduce the paper exactly, the repository ships the vintages used, with attribution to their authors; by default the pipeline downloads only the VIX, whose historical daily values are not revised. `data/raw/SHA256SUMS.txt` records the SHA-256 checksum of every raw file shipped (`cd data/raw && sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS.txt`). The VIX is not redistributed: `src/01_fetch_fred.py` downloads it and reports whether its daily values through 2026-09-22 match those used in the paper.
